proposals.test:
(0) Check the 206 NETDATA files, no training:
- the spread of median(d3)/median(d_full) across geometries;
- the weak fraction under the absolute threshold;
- the fraction of elements with |M/vol| > 1, or violating M_200*M_000 >= M_100^2, as a function of vf.

If the median ratio varies by more than 2x, or more than 0.1% of moments are invalid, then (a) and (c) matter.

(1) Two step-2 arms, both with G1a, same initialization, 20k steps:
- Control.
- G3.

Pass:
- val force and support means at least 15% lower, or the train-val gap at least 25% smaller;
- train probes within +5%;
- evalnet 'uniform' stress-test sensitivity not worse.

Arm vs control, 20k steps, same initialization and seeds.

Pass:
- val force and support means at least 10% lower;
- train-val gap at least 20% smaller;
- train probes within +5%;
- smoothness: for 3 val geometries with teacher runs at tau and tau +- 0.02 e_c for each corner c, e_hat/e* on 64 force directions changes by at most 1.5x between neighbouring perturbations.

Run only if the G1 step-0 diagnosis puts at least 40% of zero-shot error energy in weak elements plus GP.

Arm vs control, 20k steps. Measure:
- diag_error.py shares on 3 val geometries;
- the evalnet 'uniform' stress test on r2 and one val cut geometry;
- val per class.

Pass: GP+weak share -30%, stress-test sensitivity -30%, val class means within +3%.

(0) Now, no training. Copy zs_eval.py and add r_I = (C @ u)[I], w = D_II^-1 r_I and Δ_J. Run it on:
- the 3 step-1 networks on their own geometries;
- the 6 zero-shot pairs of dossier §5;
- the step-2 10k checkpoint on the 20 validation geometries.
Report the rigor check max(Δ_J/Δ) <= 1 + 1e-6, and the median/p10 of Δ_J/Δ per class.
Pass as a failure flag: every geometry with mean force error > 30% has median Δ_J >= 0.03 (certified >= 3% excess energy), and no step-1 network is flagged on its own geometry.

(1) After the head is trained, on the 20 validation + 38 test geometries:
- median Δ_lb/Δ >= 0.5 and p10 >= 0.2 for force/support/face;
- the screened μ_lb,max vs the exact ritz_top from Geo.adversarial: Spearman >= 0.8, and every geometry with ritz_top >= 2 gets μ_lb,max >= 1.3.

(2) In evalnet, report Σ_c Δ_lb,c / C_hat next to the realized compliance error on every gate load. It must be <= the realized error on 100% of loads (rigor) and >= 0.3x the realized error (sharpness).

Equivalence against the current fastnet in the style of t_fast.py, on r1, r2, FULL and the largest (430k-DOF) geometry:
- energy relative difference <= 1e-5;
- adjoint identity <= 1e-5;
- field <= 3e-4 (the current fp32 floor).

evalnet with FASTNET=1: gate numbers equal to 1e-4 relative, identical PCG iterations.

Benchmarks:
- resident memory per cell <= 0.35 GB for a FULL-size cell;
- 16 cells x 9 directions batched vs sequential: at least 2x faster;
- single-direction latency: r1 <= 2 ms, r2 <= 5 ms.

Extend lattice3 with a BDD preconditioner (rigid coarse space per cell). Compare three solvers on r1, r2 and FULL, configurations x and y:
(a) the current dense-Cholesky PCG;
(b) BDD with exact local Neumann solves (C.neumann, fp64);
(c) BDD with M_c.

Pass:
- gate numbers of (c) equal to (a) within 1e-6 relative;
- iterations of (c) <= 1.5x iterations of (b), and <= 60.

Then repeat on a 3-4 cell chain.

reviews.modification:
Run one merged oracle on r2 and 4 step-2 geometries, all 5 classes, with three arms:
(a) L3's fixed C (Q2 root and least-squares affine);
(b) P3's best local linear map;
(c) a local exact patch (ceiling).

Implement L3's fixed C with a learned scalar gate if (a) <= ~0.5% excess. Use P3's learned Phi only if (a) fails and (b) passes. If (b) also fails, the fringe is non-local: stop.

Defer. Proceed only if all three hold after G1a and augmentation:
- step-2 val shows held-out error concentrated in force/support;
- diag_error on val geometries shows the error is smooth (smooth_energy_share > 0.5);
- the gap persists.

Then test G2b alone (coarse hyperedges at 33^3 only, β zero-initialized) as one continuation arm. G2a (geometry U-Net, merged with L7b) becomes a separate later arm. Run the multi-component-voxel fraction now; it is CPU only.

Merge with D1's zero-parameter version into one zs_eval extension that reports, per direction and class:
- Δ_J (m = 1);
- the block-Jacobi Krylov lower bound (m = 8 and 16);
- the e_GL baseline test;
- the lower-bound efficiency.

Defer the curriculum, rescue and learned-head uses. Keep the Krylov steps strictly inside the monitor, labelled as such.

Trainer v2:
- swap every ~100 steps (about 4 passes in 60k), pool 3 with the DOF cap, async host prefetch;
- adversarial on first visit only, cached with the slot, and on later visits refreshed by an S_hat-only Rayleigh-Ritz step or obj-P3's bank-span adversary;
- stratified class counts per batch;
- weight EMA;
- validate() extended with sensitivity mean/p90 and per-family numbers;
- a fixed stratified probe (e.g. every 12th geometry of the order), with steps-since-visit logged.

Defer mining. Test 0 = post-hoc eval of snapshotted v1 checkpoints on early-visited vs recently-visited training geometries. Compare v2 with the v1 run at equal steps under the same 60k schedule; no separate control run is needed.

Merge into trainer v2:
- a per-geometry host buffer of 16-32 vectors;
- a seeded power-iteration refresh on first visit;
- an S_hat-only Rayleigh-Ritz refresh on later visits.

Add held-out mu on 5 val geometries at each eval. Judge it as part of the trainer v2 arm.
